0;;T;desk.POST /orders prices the lines, draws the shelf down and records a line;0;;T;desk.an order the shelf cannot cover writes nothing and says which sku;0;;T;desk.a rolled-back placement consumes the order number it was given;0;;T;desk.two lines for one sku are one reservation, and are refused as one;0;;T;desk.an order naming nothing on the shelf is refused before anything is written;0;;T;desk.a body that does not fit the type is refused by field and reason;0;;T;desk.an empty order and a line with no quantity are refused without a transaction;0;;T;desk.DELETE /orders/{id} puts the lines back and cancels once;0;;T;desk.a route nobody serves is 404 and a method nobody serves is 405 with Allow;0;;T;desk.GET /health is 200 with no store, no clock and no stop flag in reach;0;;T;desk.GET /ready is 200 when the store answers and nobody has asked it to stop;0;;T;desk.GET /ready is 503 when the store is unreachable and /health is still 200;0;;T;desk.a draining desk answers 503 before it stops accepting, and asks no database;0;;T;desk.an unset credential refuses, an empty one refuses, and a wrong one refuses;0;;T;desk.POST /orders takes the configured key and refuses every other request;0;;T;desk.a desk with no credential configured refuses POST /orders rather than accepting it;0;;T;desk.the configured credential appears in no response, no field and no record;0;;T;desk.the schema declares the key the desk cannot start without, and defaults the rest;0;;T;desk.a desk told nothing about its port refuses to start and says which flag to pass;0;;T;desk.a connection budget that is absent defaults and one that is zero refuses;0;;T;desk.a signal drains the accept loop with no source change;0;;T;desk.during the drain lead a desk is unready and still serving;0;;T;desk.a receipt is produced one line at a time and ends;0;;T;desk.GET /orders/{id}/receipt streams, and a missing order does not;0;;T;desk.a request over the simulated socket is answered and the connection closed;0;;T;desk.two pipelined requests are answered in order on one connection;0;;T;desk.a head whose terminator is split across two reads is still found;0;;T;desk.a posted order travels the whole connection and moves the store;0;;T;desk.a receipt is written as chunks and ends with the terminating chunk;0;;T;desk.HEAD is answered like GET with the length it would have had and no body;0;;T;desk.OPTIONS * answers the methods the table declares anywhere;0;;T;desk.a peer that opens a connection and says nothing is closed without a response;0;;T;desk.the service answers the same bytes over a TLS listener as over a plain one;0;;T;desk.a listener serves exactly the connections it was asked for;0;;T;desk.run_memory serves the desk with no database bound and no host at all;0;;T;desk.Content-Length and Transfer-Encoding together are refused and nothing is read;0;;T;desk.two Content-Length lines are refused even when they agree;0;;T;desk.a Content-Length that is not one or more ASCII digits is refused;0;;T;desk.a Content-Length past this service's max_body is refused before a body byte;0;;T;desk.a transfer coding that is not chunked, and one that is not last, are refused;0;;T;desk.a bare LF terminator, an obs-fold and a space before a colon are each refused;0;;T;desk.HTTP/1.1 with no Host, and with two, are each refused;0;;T;desk.a version that is not 1.0 or 1.1 is 505, and no version at all is 400;0;;T;desk.an authority-form target and a lone asterisk under GET are each refused;0;;T;desk.a chunk size that is empty, not hex, or unterminated is refused;0;;T;desk.trailers arrive in their own field and are never merged into the headers;0;;T;desk.a request line longer than this service will hold is 414;0;;T;desk.more header bytes than this service will hold is 431;0;;L;desk.every endpoint the desk can dispatch is reachable through the table;e:desk.Endpoint;0;0;;L;desk.no two routes overlap ambiguously, and every pattern is well formed;;0;0;;L;desk.a streamed receipt is byte-for-byte what a buffere